Answer "no art" and unserved Subsonic calls without HTTP 404.

Why: a WAF in front of the server (CrowdSec's http-probing: more than 10
distinct 404 URIs in 10 s) banned the operator's own IPs three times on
2026-10-24/25, every *.xarif.de service at once. Every 404 came from ordinary
use of music.xarif.de:
- the web UI's album grid: /api/v3/library/albums/{id}/artwork answered 404
  for each album without art (alert 80482: 11 such 404s);
- a signed-in Subsonic client: getCoverArt for ids the library no longer has
  (albums merged by a rescan) answered a text 404, and getPodcasts,
  getNewestPodcasts, getInternetRadioStations were unknown methods (404).
Changes:
- cover endpoints (release-group, release, artist, album artwork, library
  artist artwork) answer a missing picture with 204 + x-cover-state: missing;
  the web UI treats 204 like 404 (settled miss, no polling);
- Subsonic getCoverArt answers any miss (unknown or retired id included)
  with the neutral placeholder the playlists already use;
- getPodcasts / getNewestPodcasts / getInternetRadioStations answer empty
  lists. Unknown methods stay a plain 404 (Navidrome 0.62.0 parity, pinned by
  upstream's golden test), and an unauthenticated call still gets HTTP 200
  with code 10/40, so anonymous probing stays visible to a WAF.
- OpenAPI snapshot and generated TypeScript refreshed (5 responses 404->204).

Tests: catalog cover tests now expect 204; Subsonic cover test expects the
placeholder for unknown ids; new test for the empty lists plus anonymous code
10; new vitest spec for the frontend's missing-art check. Each fails without
its source change. Full suites (library, catalog, compat, lib units) with a
symlink-free TMPDIR on macOS: same failures with and without the patch series
(compat's symfonium journey is flaky on both: 1/5 vs 2/5). svelte-check 0
errors, prettier and eslint clean.

Remove when: upstream stops answering 404 for missing art and these calls.

